From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Benjamin Larsson <benjamin.larsson@genexis.eu>
Date: Sat, 19 Apr 2025 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mt76: add EN7523 NPU WiFi RX offload support

The Airoha EN7523 SoC contains a Network Processing Unit (NPU) that can
offload WiFi RX processing from the host CPU.  In this mode the WiFi
chip's DMA ring is redirected to NPU-internal SRAM; the NPU performs
BA reordering and PPE lookup, then writes completed frames into a
host-allocated output ring (the "host-adapter" ring).  The host reads
that ring from its NAPI handler.

This patch adds the plumbing needed for mt7915/mt7916 PCIe cards to
work in this mode when an Airoha NPU is present:

  mt76.h        – add npu_rx_process drv-op hook; called in shared
                  mt76_dma_rx_poll before falling back to standard
                  DMA ring processing
  dma.c         – invoke npu_rx_process when set in mt76_dma_rx_poll
  mt7915.h      – add npu pointer, band index, BAR0 phys base, and
                  host-adapter ring tracking to mt7915_dev; include
                  airoha_offload.h; declare new helpers
  pci.c         – obtain NPU reference from PCIe bridge OF node on
                  probe; release it on remove; store BAR0 physical addr
  mmio.c        – mt7915_mmio_npu_init(): send mailbox sequence
                  (DRIVER_MODEL, PCIE_PORT_TYPE, PCIE_ADDR, DESC,
                  init_reserved_memory, NPU_INIT_DONE), read back
                  RXDESC_BASE and write it to the WiFi DMA register,
                  allocate the host-adapter ring, register NPU WLAN IRQ;
                  mt7915_npu_rx_process(): drain host-adapter ring and
                  pass frames to the normal rx_skb path; re-enable the
                  NPU IRQ in mt7915_rx_poll_complete when NPU is active
  mt7915/dma.c  – call mt7915_mmio_npu_init() between NAPI setup and
                  DMA enable; free host-adapter ring in dma_cleanup

Requires the EN7523 PCIe nodes to carry airoha,npu = <&npu> in the DTS
(so airoha_npu_get(pdev->bus->bridge) can find the NPU), and the NPU
ring API patch (936-0-net-airoha-npu-Add-WiFi-RX-ring-management-API).

Signed-off-by: Benjamin Larsson <benjamin.larsson@genexis.eu>
---
--- a/dma.c
+++ b/dma.c
@@ -1081,7 +1081,17 @@
 	rcu_read_lock();
 
 	do {
-		cur = mt76_dma_rx_process(dev, &dev->q_rx[qid], budget - done);
+		if (dev->drv->npu_rx_process) {
+			cur = dev->drv->npu_rx_process(dev, qid,
+						       budget - done);
+			if (cur < 0)
+				cur = mt76_dma_rx_process(dev,
+							  &dev->q_rx[qid],
+							  budget - done);
+		} else {
+			cur = mt76_dma_rx_process(dev, &dev->q_rx[qid],
+						  budget - done);
+		}
 		mt76_rx_poll_complete(dev, qid, napi);
 		done += cur;
 	} while (cur && done < budget);
